0001   0000             ; .COMMENTCHAR (and .LOCALLABELCHAR) take the operand's SECOND character,
0002   0000             ; unvalidated and with no closing quote required . Here the operand
0003   0000             ; is the bare pair "Q!", so the second character '!' becomes the column-1
0004   0000             ; comment character -- the 'Q' is ignored, and there are no quotes. A single
0005   0000             ; change keeps pass 1 and pass 2 consistent. Verified byte-for-byte against the
0006   0000             ; 2001 release binary: the '!' line emits nothing, so the object is 01 02.
0007   0000                     .org 0
0008   0000                     .commentchar Q!
0009   0000             !this whole line is a comment now and emits nothing
0010   0000 01                  .byte 1
0011   0001 02                  .byte 2
0012   0002                     .end
